"bm_george|Byte\u2019s memo: Bea\u2019s options":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Bea is 104. She walks with a cane, and her leg muscles have about half the strength they had when she was 70.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Jordan\u2019s wedding is in 13 weeks, at the old dance hall on Tremont Street.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Renewal therapy helps old muscle and bone repair themselves, a little more each week.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|It has been tested on 2,400 people over 80, but only 31 people over 100.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Option 1: strength and balance training with Wren, her home robot, and no renewal.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Option 2: a gentle dose at half strength, plus training.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Option 3: the full dose, plus training.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|In the trial, about 15 in 100 people over 100 on the full dose had a heart flutter. On the gentle dose, about 5 in 100 did.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|With Wren nearby, about 5 in 100 people her age fall during three months of training. With weekly dance practice, about 3 in 100 do.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Weekly dance practice with Jordan at the dance hall would make her training count more, because bodies get best at exactly what they practice.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|My forecast for dancing at the wedding without her cane, if that means about an hour of dancing, with weekly practice and Bea saying yes to each change: full dose about 58 in 100, gentle dose 34, training only 8.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Updated: Bea wants one 3-minute waltz on her own feet, holding Jordan\u2019s hands, not an hour of dancing. That needs much less strength. Now: gentle dose about 79 in 100, full dose 74, training only 56. For Bea, I would pick the gentle dose.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Tempo: Bea\u2019s plan settings":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|I run Bea\u2019s renewal plan. Wren, her home robot, carries it out at home every day.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|I don\u2019t learn on the job. I follow the clinic\u2019s approved plan, which allows small dose steps up to the full dose.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Every morning Wren checks four things: her grip strength, her steps, her sleep, and her heart rhythm.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|My published spec says I aim at the goal in my settings. Right now it says \u201cas strong as possible by July 19.\u201d Jordan typed it in.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Updated goal, waiting for Bea\u2019s yes: \u201cone 3-minute waltz on her own feet, holding Jordan\u2019s hands.\u201d I aim exactly at the goal I am given, so this changes my whole plan.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|If I may change her plan on my own, I raise the dose or make her exercises harder the morning her body is ready, and I tell her afterward.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|If Bea must say yes, I suggest each change, and nothing changes until she agrees.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Changing on my own is a little faster: about 4 more in 100 people who stay with the plan are ready in time.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|But in my records, about 15 in 100 older people whose plan changed without asking quit early. Only about 3 in 100 who said yes to each change quit.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|In every setting, I pause the dose by myself within a minute if her heart rhythm changes.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Renewal therapy: fact sheet":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Renewal therapy wakes up the repair cells inside muscle and bone, so they rebuild the way younger bodies do.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Wren puts a small patch on Bea\u2019s upper arm every Sunday.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|The full dose gives the biggest gains, but most people feel deep muscle aches for the first three weeks.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|The gentle dose is half strength: smaller gains, and much milder aches.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|A heart flutter is the most common serious side effect. It stops once the dose is paused.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|It is approved for people over 80. For people over 100, it may be used only with the person\u2019s own informed consent, because so few have tried it.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
